.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	chateauCDProductMIB	This MIB defines Nodes and Data Objects to support Chateau Systems CD Players. This MIB has been distributed as part of the handout materials from the SNMP Technology Seminar presented by Chateau Systems. Any person or organization making use of this example MIB is responsible for ensuring its complete suitability for their own purposes. This includes the text of the legal disclaimers below, as well as all other aspects. Chateau Systems reserves the right to make changes in specifications and other information contained in this document without prior notice. The reader should contact Chateau Systems to determine whether or not such changes have been made. In no event shall Chateau Systems be liable for any incidental, indirect, special, or consequential damages whatsoever (including but not limited to lost profits) arising out of or related to this document or the information contained in it, even if Chateau Systems has been advised of, known, or should have known, the possibility of such damages. Chateau Systems grants vendors, end-users, and other interested parties a non-exclusive license to use this specification in connection with the management of Chateau Systems products. Copyright November 2005 Chateau Systems, Inc.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.1	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	chateauCDProdConfig	CD Configuration Organizational node
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.1.1	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdStaticConfig	CD Static Configuration Node
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.1.1.1	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdStCfgManufacturer	The IANA issued Enterprise OID for this Product's Manufacturer.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.1.1.10	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdStCfgFirmwareRev	The Firmware Revision for currently loaded firmware
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.1.1.2	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdStCfgModel	Manufacturer's Model Designation
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.1.2	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdDynamicConfig	CD Dynamic Configuration Node
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.1.2.1	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdDynCfgUserAlias	Any user assigned name for this CD player
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.10	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	chateauCDProdEvents	CD Player Event Data and Trap Definitions are organized under this node.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.10.0	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdEventList	Notification Objects are organized under this node.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.10.0.10	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdChassisTempAlarmEv	Sent when cdChStTemperature > cdChassisTempAlarmThresh. Will not be resent until cdChStTemperature drops below cdChasisTempAlarmThresh less 10%. This trap can be disabled by setting cdChassisTempEvTrapEn = trapDisable.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.10.0.11	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdChassisTempOkayEv	Sent when cdChStTemperature drops below cdChassisTempAlarmThresh. This trap can be disabled by setting cdChassisTempEvTrapEn = trapDisable.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.10.0.20	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdPowerSupplyEv	Sent when cdChStPowerSupply changes from okay to voltageError, or from voltageError to okay. This trap can be disabled by setting cdPowerSupplyEvTrapEn = trapDisable.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.10.1	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdEventControl	Node for data affecting Agent Trap Management Semantics
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.10.1.1	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdEvCtlAgtPollFreq	How often the Agent polls the CD Player for trappable conditions. Set = 0 to disable all traps. Persistent through system resets.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.10910.2.2.3.1.1.10.1.10	CHATEAU-CD-PRODUCT-MIB	cdChassisTempEvTrapEn	User settable to disable/enable Chassis Temperature alarms and okay events. Persistent through system resets.
