.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1	ExaltComProducts	productsMIB	Exalt devices
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.1	ExaltComProducts	productsMIBNotifications	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2	ExaltComProducts	productsMIBObjects	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1	ExaltComProducts	radioInfo	Common Radio Information to all Exalt devices.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.1	ExaltComProducts	modelName	A descriptive name for the Radio. See Web, Radio Information, Model Name.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.11	ExaltComProducts	rdkDbVer	The Device RDK Database Version. See Web, Radio Information, RDK Database Version.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.12	ExaltComProducts	txFreqRange	The Radio Tx Frequency Range. FDD radios have a Tx and Rx frequency range. See Web, Radio Information, RF Transmit range. TDD radios have one frequency range. See Web, Radio Information, RF Frequency Band.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.13	ExaltComProducts	rxFreqRange	The Radio Rx Frequency Range. FDD radios have a Tx and Rx frequency range. See Web, Radio Information, RF Receive range. TDD radios have one frequency range. See Web, Radio Information, RF Frequency Band.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.14	ExaltComProducts	rfFreqBand	The Device Frequency Band (Range). TDD radios have N/A value in this field. FDD radios have TX High or TX Low depending on used diplexer and Transmit frequency. See Web, Radio Information, Tx Band.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.15	ExaltComProducts	hwId	The Device Hardware ID number. See Web, Radio Information, Hardware ID number
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.16	ExaltComProducts	modelNumber	The Model Number of the Radio. See Web, Radio Information, Model Number
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.2	ExaltComProducts	partNumber	The Part Number of the Radio. See Web, Radio Information, Part Number.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.3	ExaltComProducts	serialNumber	The Radio Serial Number. See Web, Radio Inforamtion, Serial Number.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.4	ExaltComProducts	interfaceType	The Interfaces available on this radio. Ethernet, T1/E1, etc. See Web, Radio Information, Interface Type.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.5	ExaltComProducts	firmwareVersion	The Radio Firmware Version. See Web, Radio Information, Firmware Version.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1.6	ExaltComProducts	bootVersion	The Radio Boot Code Version. See Web, Radio Information, Boot Version.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.1000	ExaltComProducts	radioReboot	Reboot the radio device. Send 'reboot' to radioReboot parameter to reboot the radio device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2	ExaltComProducts	radioAdmin	Radio Administration parameters.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.1	ExaltComProducts	sysDate	The Radio System Date, MM/DD/YYYY. See Web, Administration, Settings, Date. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change. After commit, SNMP restarts and will be down for 30 seconds.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.10	ExaltComProducts	ipAddressNetmask	The IP address and Subnet Mask of local radio. ie 10.0.0.1/24. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.1000	ExaltComProducts	commitAdminSettings	The Commit Administration settings command. Valid values: 'save', 'clear'. Configuration changes via SNMP do not take effect until 'save' (Commit) command is sent to this parameter. 'clear' (Cancel) command is used to cancel configuration changes before commit operation. In case of invalid configuration this parameter contains text description of the problem.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.11	ExaltComProducts	defaultGateway	The Default Gateway for local radio port. See Web, Administration, Settings, Default Gateway. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.12	ExaltComProducts	aesEnable	The AES enable(0)/disable(1). AES (Advance Encryption Standard) can be implemented to provide additional data security for the wireless link. This function requires an upgrade license key (purchased separately). See Web, Administration, Settings, AES Settings, Enable AES. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.13	ExaltComProducts	aesKey	The symmetric AES key for encrypt/decrypt payload data. Different bitlength encryption license keys (for example, 128-bit and 256-bit) are available, depending on model type and license type. AES Key should match both on local radio and far end radio. See Web, Administration, Settings, AES Settings, AES Key. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.14	ExaltComProducts	licKey	The license key which defines radio features and capabilities. See Web, Administration, Settings, License Key. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17	ExaltComProducts	snmpConfig	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.1	ExaltComProducts	trapIpaddr	The IP address to which the SNMP traps are directed. See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Trap Destination IP Address.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.10	ExaltComProducts	trapv1Enable	SNMPv1 Traps enable(0)/disable(1). Enables traps for SNMP protocol version 1. See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Enable SNMPv1 Traps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.11	ExaltComProducts	trapv2cEnable	SNMPv2c Traps enable(0)/disable(1). Enables traps for SNMP protocol version 2c. See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Enable SNMPv2c Traps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.12	ExaltComProducts	trapv3Enable	SNMPv3 Traps enable(0)/disable(1). Enables traps for SNMP protocol version 3. See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Enable SNMPv3 Traps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.2	ExaltComProducts	trapAuth	Authentication trap enable(1)/disable(0). This is an SNMP standard trap when password information for SNMP is incorrect. See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Authentication Trap.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.3	ExaltComProducts	trapReboot	Reboot trap enable(0)/disable(1). This trap is sent after any radio reboot to inform the manager of the reboot status. See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Radio Reboot Trap.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.4	ExaltComProducts	trapLocLinkStat	Local Link Status trap enable(0)/disable(1). This trap is sent when Link is in errored state (equivalent to the Link LED). See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Local Link Status Trap.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.5	ExaltComProducts	trapLocAlarmStat	Local Alarm Status trap enable(0)/disable(1). This trap is sent when local radio Status is in errored state (equivalent to the Status LED). See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Local Radio Status Trap.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.6	ExaltComProducts	trapRemAlarmStat	Remote Alarm Status trap enable(0)/disable(1). This trap is sent when remote radio Status is in errored state (equivalent to the Status LED). See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Remote Radio Status Trap.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.7	ExaltComProducts	trapLocRslStat	Local RSL Status trap enable(0)/disable(1). This trap is sent when the local RSL drops below the value set in the RSL Threshold Value (dBm) field. See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Local RSL Status Trap.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.8	ExaltComProducts	trapLocTempStat	Local Temperature Status trap enable(0)/disable(1). This trap is sent when the internal temperature reaches the warning point. See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Temperature Status Trap.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.17.9	ExaltComProducts	trapLocRslThreshold	Local RSL Threshold. Exalt recommends that this trap be set to a value 5dBm or 10dBm above the threshold as a warning that the system has faded and may be approaching an outage. See Web, Administration, SNMP, Traps, Threshold Value.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.18	ExaltComProducts	ntp	NTP and Time zone configuration.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.18.1	ExaltComProducts	ntpClientEnable	this mib to enable/disable the NTP client in the radio. 0 - disable NTP client. 1 - enable with 1 NTP server. 2 - enable with 2 NTP servers. 3 - enable with 3 NTP servers. 4 - enable with 4 NTP servers.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.18.1000	ExaltComProducts	commitNtpSettings	This command allows saving or clear the NTP and Tome Zone configuration. If the save includes the change of time zone, the radio will automatically reboot to take effect the newly selected time zone. Option strings to be written are: save, clear, correspondingly saving changes to configuration to the persistent storage or clearing unsaved changes.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.18.2	ExaltComProducts	ntpServer1IpAddr	IP address for the first NTP server in xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx format
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.18.3	ExaltComProducts	ntpServer2IpAddr	IP address for the second NTP server in xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx format
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.18.4	ExaltComProducts	ntpServer3IpAddr	IP address for the third NTP server in xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx format
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.18.5	ExaltComProducts	ntpServer4IpAddr	IP address for the forth NTP server in xxx.xxx.xxx.xxx format
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.18.6	ExaltComProducts	ntpTimeZoneSelect	Time Zone selection. 0 - (GMT-11:00) Samoa 1 - (GMT-10.00) Hawaii 2 - (GMT-09:00) Alaska 3 - (GMT-08:00) Pacific Time 4 - (GMT-07:00) Arizona 5 - (GMT-07:00) Montain Time 6 - (GMT-06:00) Central Time 7 - (GMT-05:00) Eastern Time 8 - (GMT-05:00) Indiana (East) 9 - (GMT-04:00) Atlantic Time (Canada) 10- (GMT) Coordinated Universal Time 11- (GMT) London 12- (GMT+01:00) Berlin 13- (GMT+01:00) Belgrade 14- (GMT+01:00) Paris 15- (GMT+02:00) Cairo 16- (GMT+02:00) Helsinki 17- (GMT+03:00) Baghdad 18- (GMT+03:00) Moscow 19- (GMT+03:30) Tehran 20- (GMT+04:30) Kabul 21- (GMT+05:00) Karachi 22- (GMT+07:00) Bangkok 23- (GMT+08:00) Shanghai 24- (GMT+08:00) Taipei 25- (GMT+09:00) Tokyo 26- (GMT+09:00) Seoul 27- (GMT+10:00) Sydney 28- (GMT+10:00) Vladivostok
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.2	ExaltComProducts	sysTime	The Radio System Time, HH:MM:SS, as 24 hours. See Web, Administration, Settings, Time. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change. After commit, SNMP restarts and will be down for 30 seconds.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.3	ExaltComProducts	radioName	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.3.1	ExaltComProducts	rnLocal	The user specifiable Radio Name for this radio. See Web, Administration, Settings, Radio Name. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.3.2	ExaltComProducts	rnRemote	The Radio Name of the Radio at the far end of this RF Link. Can only be set at that radio. See Web, Administration, Settings, Radio Name.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.4	ExaltComProducts	linkName	The user specifiable Link Name for this radio. See Web, Administration, Settings, Link Name. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.5	ExaltComProducts	linkSecKey	The Link Security Key must match on both ends of an RF Link for traffic to pass. See Web, Administration, Settings, Link Security Key. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.6	ExaltComProducts	adminPassword	The password for admin login to Web/CLI. See Web, Administration, Settings, Admin Password. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.7	ExaltComProducts	userPassword	The password for user login to Web/CLI. See Web, Administration, Settings, User Password. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.8	ExaltComProducts	ipAddress	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.8.1	ExaltComProducts	ipLocal	The IP address of local radio. This IP address is used to manage radio. See Web, Administration, Settings, IP Address. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.8.2	ExaltComProducts	ipRemote	The IP address of the remote Radio. This IP address is used to manage Remote radio. Can only be set at that radio. See Web, Administration, Settings, IP Address.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.2.9	ExaltComProducts	subnetMask	The Subnet Mask for IP address of local radio. See Web, Administration, Settings, IP Mask. To make permanent, write save to commitAdminSettings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3	ExaltComProducts	radioConfig	The Radio Configuration Section.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.1	ExaltComProducts	systemConfig	This is the device specific configuration section.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.1.1000	ExaltComProducts	commitSystemSettings	The Commit System Configuration settings command. Valid values: 'save', 'clear'. Configuration changes via SNMP do not take effect until 'save' (Commit) command is sent to this parameter. 'clear' (Cancel) command is used to cancel configuration changes before commit operation. In case of invalid configuration this parameter contains text description of the problem.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2	ExaltComProducts	interface	Radio Interfaces Configuration section.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2	ExaltComProducts	te1	T1,E1 interfaces Configuration section. Section allows to configure T1/E1 ports on the radio if any.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.1	ExaltComProducts	te1NumChannels	The Number of T1 or E1 channels supported by the Radio.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.1000	ExaltComProducts	commitTe1Settings	The Commit TE1 Configuration settings command. Valid values: 'save', 'clear'. Configuration changes to TE1 ports via SNMP do not take effect until 'save' (Commit) command is sent to this parameter. 'clear' (Cancel) command is used to cancel configuration changes before commit operation. In case of invalid configuration this parameter contains text description of the problem.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.2	ExaltComProducts	te1NumActiveChannels	The Current number of channels available, based on bandwitdh of the RF link and the license key.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.3	ExaltComProducts	selectT1orE1	Select operation mode of T1/E1 interfaces. Either T1(0) or E1(1). See Web, Configuration, Interface, T1/E1, Set To E1/T1 Mode button.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.4	ExaltComProducts	te1Interfaces	Attributes for T1 or E1 ports.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.4.1	ExaltComProducts	te1Interface	An entry in the T1/E1 Attribute table.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.4.1.1	ExaltComProducts	te1Status	The T1/E1 status: enable(1)/disable(0). Parameter allows to enable/disable each individual T1 channel. See Web, Configuration, Interface, T1/E1, Status. To make permanent, write save to commitTe1Settings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.4.1.2	ExaltComProducts	t1LBO	The Line Build Out length range. Valid values (ft): lbo0to133(0), lbo133to266(1), lbo266to399(2), lbo399to533(3), lbo533to655(4). See Web, Configuration, Interface, T1/E1, LBO. To make permanent, write save to commitTe1Settings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.4.1.3	ExaltComProducts	te1AIS	The T1/E1 AIS enabled flag: enable(1)/disable(0). If enabled, the radio places an AIS code on the output of the associated interface if and when the link fails or when there is no E1 signal available from the far end to provide the user at the local end. See Web, Configuration, Interface, T1/E1, AIS. To make permanent, write save to commitTe1Settings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.4.1.4	ExaltComProducts	t1LineCode	The T1/E1 Line Code type: b8zs(0), ami(1). See Web, Configuration, Interface, T1/E1, AIS, Line Code. To make permanent, write save to commitTe1Settings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.2.2.4.1.5	ExaltComProducts	te1LoopBackMode	The Loop Back Mode for a T1/E1 interface. Valid values: disabled(0), ExternalLocal(1), ExternalRemote(2), Internal(3). All loopback configurations control the loop at the Line Interface integrated circuit, which is the device wired directly to the front panel ports. See Web, Configuration, Interface, T1/E1, AIS, Loopback. To make permanent, write save to commitTe1Settings after change.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3	ExaltComProducts	fileManagement	The File Management Section. This section allows to initiate Upload/Download firmware/configuration/logs, perform Firmware activation procedure.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3.1	ExaltComProducts	currentFwFilename	The file name of the currently running firmware. See Web, Administration, File Management, File Activation, Current File.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3.2	ExaltComProducts	alternateFwFilename	The file name of the alternate firmware image. See Web, Administration, File Management, File Activation, Alternative File.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3.3	ExaltComProducts	swapFWimage	Swap the firmware images and restart radio. To perform swap operation 'swap' command needs to be sent to this parameter. For ExtendAirG2 to perform revert to factory operation 'factory' command needs to be sent. Radio will become unavailable for several minutes.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3.4	ExaltComProducts	fileTransfer	The File Transfer Section. This section allows to initiate Upload/Download firmware/configuration/logs over TFTP protocol.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3.4.1	ExaltComProducts	tftpServerIp	The TFTP Server IP address. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3.4.2	ExaltComProducts	uploadFilename	The name of the file for upload operation. For configuration file uploadFilename should be always 'config.xml'. uploadFilename value should match the file name in TFTP server folder.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3.4.3	ExaltComProducts	transferType	The file transfer type. Valid values: - uploadFirmware(0) - uploadConfig(1) - uploadRDD(2) (Valid only for TDD radios) - downloadFirmware(3) - downloadConfig(4) - downloadMIBs(5) - downloadEventLogs(6). The actual operation starts via updating transferStart parameter value.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3.4.4	ExaltComProducts	transferStart	TransferStart parameter is used to initiate file transfer operation. Send startTransfer(1) to this parameter.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3.4.5	ExaltComProducts	transferStatus	The current file transfer status.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.3.3.5	ExaltComProducts	factoryFwFilename	The file name of the factory firmware image. See Web, Administration, File Management, File Activation, Factory File.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.25651.1.2.4	ExaltComProducts	radioMonitor	Monitor Various components.
