.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.18.3.1	C-PRODUCT-MCPU-MIB	shaperTable	The shaper Table contains up to 15 shapers rate. This table uses cardSlot and Shaper number as an index which is uniquely assoicate to entry of each shaper. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.18.3.1.1	C-PRODUCT-MCPU-MIB	shaperEntry	Each entry in the table contains the information of a shaper.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.18.3.1.1.1	C-PRODUCT-MCPU-MIB	shaperNumber	Shaper Number of a frame based card
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.18.3.1.1.2	C-PRODUCT-MCPU-MIB	shaperSustainableCellRateInbps	Sustainable Cell Rate (SCR), in bits per second, is an upper bound on the conforming average rate of an ATM connection over time scales.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.18.3.1.1.3	C-PRODUCT-MCPU-MIB	shaperSustainableCellRateIncps	Sustainable Cell Rate (SCR), in cells per second, is an upper bound on the conforming average rate of an ATM connection over time scales. The value is calculated based on the input from SCR in bps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.18.3.1.1.4	C-PRODUCT-MCPU-MIB	shaperPeakCellRateInbps	Peak Cell Rate (PCR), in bits per second, is the rate at which ATM source end system can send to a referenced physical service access point that is equal to the inverse of the minimum cell interarrival time. The value of Peak Rate Cell Rate (PCR) cannot be lower than Sustainable Cell Rate (SCR). 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.18.3.1.1.5	C-PRODUCT-MCPU-MIB	shaperPeakCellRateIncps	Peak Cell Rate (PCR), in cells per second, is the rate at which ATM source end system can send to a referenced physical service access point that is equal to the inverse of the minimum cell interarrival time. The value of Peak Rate Cell Rate (PCR) is calculated based on the input from PCR in bps. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.18.3.1.1.6	C-PRODUCT-MCPU-MIB	shaperMaximumBurstSizeInBits	Maximum Burst Size in bits. This value is read only and is calculated again when MBS (in cells) is changed
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.18.3.1.1.7	C-PRODUCT-MCPU-MIB	shaperMaximumBurstSizeInCells	Maximum Burst Size in cells. Minimum value is 1 cell and maximum value is 255 cells. 
