.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.10	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupAdminLinkDelayMax	This object is the group admin maximum link differential delay in msec.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.11	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupOperLinkDelayMax	This object is the operational maximum link differential delay in msec.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.12	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupAdminPortsBitMap	This bit map object indicates the ports configured for the group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.13	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupOperPortsBitMap	This bit map object indicates the operational ports in the group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.14	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupOperStatus	This object indicates the group operational service status.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.15	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupRowStatus	This object indicates the row set action request.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.2	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupImaId	This object is the admin IMA id of the group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.3	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupAdminStatus	This object indicates the admin service status of the group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.4	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupMinNumLinksStart	This object indicates the minimum number of links to start the group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.5	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupMinNumLinksFailed	This object indicates the minimum number of links for the group to stay up, links lower than this number will declare the group to fail.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.19.3.1.1.6	C-PRODUCT-IMA-MIB	imaCardGroupMaxNumLinksAct	This object indicates the maximum number of links for the group, for a trunk IMA card, the value is the imaCardGroupSize, for a port card, it is derived from the imaCardGroupAdminPortsBitMap.
