.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.1.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardBufferTable	This object contains the CTX Queue Buffer information table. There are one ctxCardBufferEntry associated for each CTX Queue. Within the shelf, there are 16 queue buffers. The table uses the slot number and queue number as an index associated with each queue buffer. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.1.1.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardBufferEntry	Information about a CTX Buffer information.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.1.1.1.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardBufferIndex	Queue Index 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.1.1.1.2	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardInterface	This object describes the Description of the queue. The queue Description is combined with slot, Card Interface, high/low priority queue. For example: Slot Interface Queue 3 IMA Grp 1 0 CBR 3 IMA Grp 1 1 VBR 3 IMA Grp 1 2 UBR1 ... (SAR ports) 1 low 8 (none) 0 high 8 (none) 1 low 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.1.1.1.3	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardBufferCells	This object indicates the buffer cells configured to a specified card interface. The integer value contains between 512 and 65280. The unit of Buffer Cells is in number of cells. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.1.1.1.4	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardCongOn	This object indicates the percentage of Congestion ON configured to a specified card interface. The integer value contains 0-100 percentage. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.1.1.1.5	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardCongOff	This object indicates the percentage of Congestion OFF configured to a specified card interface. The integer value contains 0-100 percentage. 
