.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.2.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardShapersTable	This object contains the CTX Traffic Shaper information table. There are one ctxCardShapersEntry associated for each Traffic Shaper. Within the shelf, there are total of seven Traffic Shapers. The table uses the slot number and shaper Index as an index associated for each Traffic shaper. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.2.1.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardShapersEntry	Information about a CTX Shaper information.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.2.1.1.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardShapersIndex	The Index is associated with Traffic shaper. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.2.1.1.2	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardShapersDesc	This object describes the Description of the Traffic shaper. For example: Trunk Bulk Trk Grp 1 (VBR HI) Trk Grp 1 (VBR LO) Trk Grp 1 (UBR) SAR Output SAR Input OC3 Bulk 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.2.1.1.3	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardShapersRate	This object contains the Traffic Shapers Rate. The integer value contains between 150 and 390625 for Trunk Bulk, Trk Grp and OC3 Bulk. The max Shaper rate for SAR Output/Input is 78125. The unit of Shapers Rate is in cells per seconds. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.3	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCard	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.3.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardTable	This object contains the CTX card information table. There are one ctxCardEntry associated for each CTX card. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.3.1.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardEntry	Information about a CTX Card information.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.1.3.1.1.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxCardReset	This object indicates the action to be changed CTX buffer by a reset CTX card. It will cause cell loss on all Virtual Circuits for 10ms. A read request always return zero. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.2	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxATMStats	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.2.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxATMStatsTable	This object contains the CTX specific VC Statistics table. There is one ctxATMStatsEntry associated for each CTX VC connection provisioned within the shelf. This table uses vcpSideId as an index which is defined in the vcBaseTable of the C-PRODUCT BASE MIB. This index value uniquely identifies the CTX VC connection to which this entry is applicable. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.2.1.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxATMStatsEntry	An entry in the CTX specific VC Statistics table.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.2.1.1.1	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxATMStatsRxCells	This object indicates the total number of ATM cells received over the CTX ATM VC connection since the last ATM VC clear time and date.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.2.1.1.2	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxATMStatsTxCells	This object indicates the total number of ATM cells transmitted over the CTX ATM VC connection since the last ATM VC clear time and date.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.2.1.1.3	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxATMStatsResetStats	This object will (1) clear the ATM statistics counters and (2) initialize the reset time and date to the current time and date for the specified ATM VC connection. NOTE: A value of '2' is returned for any attempted reads of this object.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.20.2.1.1.4	C-PRODUCT-CTX-MIB	ctxATMStatsResetTimeDate	This object indicates the last time and date the ATM statistics were cleared for the specified ATM VC connection.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3	C-PRODUCT-GROUP-MIB	card	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardBaseTable	A 6 entry card table in the shelf.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardBaseEntry	Each card entry contains objects that refer to the card in that entry.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1.1	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardSlot	Slot number of the card in the shelf. The assignment of the card slots is as follows: slot 1 : management cpu, slot 2 : ctx card, slot 3 : one of the trunk cards (e.g. ds3/oc3/e3/hssi), slot 4-6: one of the port cards (e.g. ether/cbr/qsim).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1.10	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardShelfState	Operational shelf state of the card.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1.2	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardTypeDb	The configured card type in the slot. It may differ from the actual card type (cardTypeHw) in the corresponding slot. A set request will be accepted only when one of the following is true: 1. the value of cardTypeHw in this slot is none, or 2. the new value of cardTypeDb is the same as the corresponding cardTypeHw. 
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1.3	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardTypeHw	The actual card type in the slot.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1.4	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardAdminStatus	Administrative status of the card. An error is returned if this slot has been selected as the system reference clock and an attempt is made to change this object to out-of-service. This object does not apply to management cpu and ctx card.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1.5	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardOperStatus	Operational status of the card.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1.6	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardSerialNumber	Serial number of the card.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1.7	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardRevision	Hardware revision number of the card.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1.8	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardPartNumber	Part number of the card.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.43.1.12.1.1.3.1.1.9	C-PRODUCT-BASE-MIB	cardReset	This is the command to reset the card at the specified slot number. A read request always returns 0. Warning: Reseting card will temporarily disrupt traffic on the specified slot number.
