.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceTable	A list of device table entries. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpDevicesNumDevices.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular device managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIndex	The table row index for the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceStatus	The currently most critical alarm status for the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceRowStatus	Used with table edits to indicate the status of a given row in tlDeviceTable.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceType	The type of device. One of the appropriate hardware types: ups, pdu, envirosense, etc.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceManufacturer	The name of the manufacturer.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceModel	The model designation.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceName	A user-supplied name for the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceID	A user-supplied ID for the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceLocation	A user-supplied location for the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.1.2.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceRegion	A user-supplied region for the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceDetail	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentTable	The identity details of each device in device table. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpDevicesNumDevices.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentEntry	An entry containing details for a particular device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentProtocol	The Tripplite protocol used to communicate with the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentCommPortType	The type of communications port used to connect with the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentCommPortName	The name of the communications port.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentFirmwareVersion	The firmware version of the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentSerialNum	The serial number of the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentDateInstalled	The installation date for this device in the format of mm/dd/yyyy.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentHardwareVersion	The hardware revision of the device. This value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME if not supported by the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentCurrentUptime	The device uptime since its last startup. The format of this value is a comma- delimited string representing days, hours and minutes. For example, the value of 123,4,5 represents 123 days, 4 hours and 5 minutes. This value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME if not supported by the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.2.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceIdentTotalUptime	The cumulative (total) uptime for the device. The format of this value is a comma- delimited string representing days, hours and minutes. For example, the value of 123,4,5 represents 123 days, 4 hours and 5 minutes. This value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME if not supported by the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpDeviceTypes	
