.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsIdentTable	The identity details of each ups in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are upss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsIdentEntry	An entry containing details for a particular ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsIdentNumInputs	The number of input lines supported by the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsIdentNumOutputs	The number of output lines supported by the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsIdentNumBypass	The number of bypass lines supported by the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsIdentNumPhases	The number of phases supported by the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsIdentNumOutlets	The number of receptacles supported by the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsIdentNumOutletGroups	The number of receptacle groups supported by the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.2.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsIdentNumBatteryPacks	The number of battery packs, internal and external combined, supported by the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsSupportsTable	The supported details of each ups in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are upss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsSupportsEntry	An entry containing supported details for a particular ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsSupportsEnergywise	Indicates whether the ups supports Cisco EnergyWise.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsSupportsRampShed	Indicates whether the ups supports ramping and shedding.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.3.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsSupportsOutletGroup	Indicates whether the ups supports outlet groups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.3.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsSupportsOutletCurrentPower	Indicates whether the ups reports individual receptacle current and power measurements. Devices that do not support individual receptacle measurements will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME for tlpUpsOutletCurrent and tlpUpsOutletPower.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.1.3.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsSupportsOutletVoltage	Indicates whether the ups reports individual receptacle voltage measurements. Devices that do not support individual receptacle measurements will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME for tlpUpsOutletVoltage.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDevice	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDeviceTable	The device details of each ups in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are upss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDeviceEntry	An entry containing device details for a particular ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDeviceMainLoadState	The current state of the main output of the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDeviceMainLoadControllable	Indicates whether or not the main output is controllable, and whether the ups can be turned off and on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDeviceMainLoadCommand	Reading this value will always return 0. Setting this value to turnOff(1) will turn off the main output of the ups. Setting this value to turnOn(2) will turn on the main output of the ups. Setting this value to cycle(3) will turn off the main output, then turn it back on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDevicePowerOnDelay	The configurable delay value, which sets the amount of additional time a given device will wait before it connects to a valid AC source. By default the delay value is set to 0.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDeviceTestDate	The date of the last self-test run on the ups, in the format YYYY-MM-DD.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDeviceTestResultsStatus	The result of the last self-test run on the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDeviceTemperatureC	The ambient temperature at or near the ups casing. Temperature measurements are not supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.2.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDeviceTemperatureF	The ambient temperature at or near the ups casing. Temperature measurements are not supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsDetail	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBattery	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatterySummaryTable	The battery system summary of each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatterySummaryEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular battery system managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryStatus	The indication of the capacity remaining in the UPS system's batteries. A value of batteryNormal indicates that the remaining run-time is greater than tlpUpsConfigLowBattTime. A value of batteryLow indicates that the remaining battery run-time is less than or equal to tlpUpsConfigLowBattTime. A value of batteryDepleted indicates that the UPS will be unable to sustain the present load when and if the utility power is lost (including the possibility that the utility power is currently absent and the UPS is unable to sustain the output).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsSecondsOnBattery	If the unit is on battery power, the elapsed time since the UPS last switched to battery power, or the time since the network management subsystem was last restarted, whichever is less. Zero shall be returned if the unit is not on battery power.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsEstimatedMinutesRemaining	An estimate of the time to battery charge depletion under the present load conditions if the utility power is off and remains off, or if it were to be lost and remain off.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsEstimatedChargeRemaining	An estimate of the battery charge remaining expressed as a percent of full charge.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryRunTimeRemaining	The run time remaining before batteries are exhausted. If the device does not support run time remaining, then the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryDetailTable	The battery detail of each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryDetailEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular battery system managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryDetailVoltage	The magnitude of the present battery voltage.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryDetailCurrent	The present battery current.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryDetailCapacity	The estimated remaining battery capacity expressed as a percent of full capacity.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryDetailCharge	Denotes the charge state of the battery.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryDetailChargerStatus	The status of the battery charger. If the device does not support this value, then the agent will report ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackIdentTable	The battery identification details for each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by upsIdentNumUps and the number of battery battery packs per each as reported by tlpUpsNumBatteryPacks.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackIdentEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular battery pack managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackIdentIndex	The table row index for the ups battery pack.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackIdentManufacturer	The manufacturer of the battery pack. If the device does not support this value, then the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.3.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackIdentModel	The model or device name of the battery pack. If the device does not support this value, then the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.3.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackIdentSerialNum	The serial number of the battery pack. If the device does not support this value, then the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.3.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackIdentFirmware	The firmware of the battery pack. If the device does not support this value, then the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.3.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackIdentSKU	The SKU of the battery pack. If the device does not support this value, then the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigTable	The battery configuration details for each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by upsIdentNumUps and the number of battery battery packs per each as reported by tlpUpsNumBatteryPacks.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular battery pack managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigChemistry	The type of battery pack.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigCellCapacity	The capacity of the batteries in the measurement defined by tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigCapacityUnits. If the device does not support this value, then the agent will report ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.11	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigMinCellVoltage	The minimum cell voltage for the batteries. If the device does not support this value, then the agent will report ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.12	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigMaxCellVoltage	The maximum cell voltage for the batteries. If the device does not support this value, then the agent will report ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigStyle	The style of battery pack.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigLocation	The location of the battery pack.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigStrings	The number of series strings in parallel contained in the battery pack. If the device does not support this value, then the agent will report ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigBatteriesPerString	The number of battery per each string in the battery pack. If the device does not support this value, then the agent will report ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigCellsPerBattery	The number of cells per battery..
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigNumBatteries	The total number of batteries contained in the battery pack. If the device does not support this value, then the agent will report ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigCapacityUnits	The units of measurement used for tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigDesignCapacity and tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigCellCapacity. If supported, this value will report either mAHR(1), amps per hour, or mWhr(1), watts per hour. If the device does not support this value, then the agent will report ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.4.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigDesignCapacity	The theoretical or nominal capacity of the battery pack in the measurement defined by tlpUpsBatteryPackConfigCapacityUnits. If the device does not support this value, then the agent will report ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackDetailTable	The details of each battery pack for each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss and battery packs managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps and tlpUpsIdentNumBatteryPacks.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.5.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackDetailEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular battery system managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.5.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackDetailCondition	The condition of the battery. A bad battery should be replaced.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.5.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackDetailTemperatureC	The ambient temperature at or near the UPS Battery casing.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.5.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackDetailTemperatureF	The ambient temperature at or near the UPS Battery casing.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.5.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackDetailAge	The age of the battery in years. This is equal to the current date minus tlpUpsBatteryPackIdentInstallDate.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.5.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackDetailLastReplaceDate	The date when the batteries were last replaced in YYYYMMDD format.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.5.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackDetailNextReplaceDate	The date when the batteries should next be replaced in YYYYMMDD format.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.1.5.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBatteryPackDetailCycleCount	The number of times the battery went into invert mode. This number is incremented by 1 each time the unit goes on battery mode (with the exception of Self Test mode). If the device does not support this value, then the agent will report ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInput	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputTable	The input details of each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputEntry	An entry containing information applicable to all input lines per each ups managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputLineBads	A count of the number of times the input entered an out-of-tolerance condition as defined by the manufacturer. This count is incremented by one each time the input transitions from zero out-of-tolerance lines to one or more input lines out-of-tolerance. This value is not supported on all units. If the ups does not support this value, then the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputNominalVoltage	The nominal value of the input line voltage. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputNominalFrequency	The nominal value of the input line frequency. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputLowTransferVoltage	The minimum line voltage allowed before the ups system transfers to battery backup.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputLowTransferVoltageLowerBound	The lower boundary value of tlpUpsInputLowTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputLowTransferVoltageUpperBound	The upper boundary value of tlpUpsInputLowTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputHighTransferVoltage	The maximum line voltage allowed before the ups system transfers to battery backup.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputHighTransferVoltageLowerBound	The lower boundary value of tlpUpsInputHighTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputHighTransferVoltageUpperBound	The upper boundary value of tlpUpsInputHighTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputPhaseTable	The input phase details of each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps and tlpUpsIdentNumPhases.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputPhaseEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular input phase managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputPhaseIndex	The table row index for the ups input phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputPhaseFrequency	The present input frequency for a given input line.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputPhaseVoltage	The magnitude of the present input voltage for a given input line.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputPhaseVoltageMin	The minimum input voltage value since the last reset of this value for a given input line. If any value is written to either tlpUpsInputVoltageMin or tlpUpsInputVoltageMax, both will be reset to their appropriate minimum and maximum values.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputPhaseVoltageMax	The maximum input voltage value since the last reset of this value for a given input line. If any value is written to either tlpUpsInputVoltageMin or tlpUpsInputVoltageMax, both will be reset to their appropriate minimum and maximum values.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputPhaseCurrent	The magnitude of the present input current.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.2.2.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsInputPhasePower	The magnitude of the present input true power.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutput	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputTable	The output details of each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular output line managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputSource	The present source of output power. The enumeration none(2) indicates that there is no source of output power (and therefore no output power), for example, the system has opened the output breaker.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputNominalVoltage	The nominal value of the output voltage. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputFrequency	The present output frequency. The output frequency on most ups devices is common across all output lines. Some ups devices, however, maintain the output frequency per each line. If a common frequency is supported by the ups, then this frequency will contain the common frequency value. If not supported, the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputLineTable	The output line details of each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputLineEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular output line managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputLineIndex	The table row index for the ups output line.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputLineVoltage	The magnitude of the present output voltage for a given output line.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputLineCurrent	The present output current.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputLinePower	The present output true power.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputLinePercentLoad	The percentage of the UPS power capacity presently being used on this output line, i.e., the greater of the percent load of true power capacity and the percent load of VA.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.3.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutputLineFrequency	The present output frequency on this output line. The output frequency on most ups devices is common across all output lines. Some ups devices, however, maintain the output frequency per each line. If a per line frequency is supported by the ups, then this frequency value will reports the value of this line. If not supported, the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBypass	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.4.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBypassTable	The bypass details of each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.4.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBypassEntry	An entry containing information applicable to all input lines per each ups managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.4.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBypassFrequency	The present bypass frequency.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.4.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBypassLineTable	The bypass line details of each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.4.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBypassLineEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular bypass line managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.4.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBypassLineIndex	The bypass line identifier.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.4.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBypassLineVoltage	The present bypass voltage.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.4.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBypassLineCurrent	The present bypass current.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.4.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsBypassLinePower	The present true power conveyed by the bypass.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutlet	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletTable	The details of each ups outlet in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular outlet managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletIndex	The table row index for the ups outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletRampAction	The ramp action to take on a given outlet when powering on the device. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpUpsOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.11	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletRampDelay	The number of seconds to delay before powering on the given outlet. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpUpsOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.12	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletShedAction	The shed action to take on a given outlet when powering off the device. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpUpsOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.13	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletShedDelay	The number of seconds to delay before powering off the given outlet. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpUpsOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.14	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletGroup	The tlpUpsOutletGroupIndex group index of the respective group to which the given outlet is assigned, or zero (0) if the given outlet is not grouped.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletName	A user-definable string identifying the name of the outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletDescription	A user-definable string identifying the device(s) connected to the given outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletState	The current state of the outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletControllable	Denotes whether this outlet is controllable.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletCommand	Reading this value will always return 0. Setting this value to turnOff(1) will turn off the outlet. Setting this value to turnOn(2) will turn on the outlet. Setting this value to cycle(3) will turn the outlet off, then turn it back on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletVoltage	The magnitude of the present output voltage for a given outlet. If the voltage measurement is not supported for an individual receptacle regardless whether device-wide or just for this receptacle, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. Device-wide support for receptacle voltage measurements is denoted by tlpUpsSupportsOutletVoltage.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletCurrent	The present output current, in hundreths of amps, of a given outlet. If the current measurement is not supported for an individual receptacle regardless whether device-wide or just for this receptacle, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. Device-wide support for receptacle current measurements is denoted by tlpUpsSupportsCurrentPower.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletPower	The output power of a given outlet. If the power measurement is not supported for an individual receptacle regardless whether device-wide or just for this receptacle, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. Device-wide support for receptacle power measurements is denoted by tlpUpsSupportsCurrentPower.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletGroupTable	The receptacle grouping details of each ups in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the value of tlpUpsIdentNumOutletGroups per each device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletGroupEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular outlet group managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletGroupIndex	The table row index for the ups outlet group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletGroupRowStatus	Row status for the tlpUpsOutletGroupTable
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletGroupName	The name of this outlet group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletGroupDescription	A description for this outlet group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletGroupState	The current state of the outlet group. This value will report off(1) if all outlets in the group are off, on(2) if all outlets in the group are on, mixed(3) if some outlets in the group are off and others are on, or unknown(0) if the state of the outlets cannot be determined.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.5.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsOutletGroupCommand	Reading this value will always return 0. Setting this value to turnOff(1) will turn off every outlet associated with the group. Setting this value to turnOn(2) will turn on every outlet associated with the group. Setting this value to cycle(3) will turn off every outlet associated with the group, then turn each outlet back on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsWatchdog	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.6.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsWatchdogTable	The watchdog details of each ups in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are upss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.6.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsWatchdogEntry	An entry containing watchdog details for a particular ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.6.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsWatchdogSupported	Indicates whether or not this ups supports a watchdog reboot.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.3.6.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsWatchdogSecsBeforeReboot	The maximum number of seconds that can expire between polls that the engine makes to the ups for data. If this time runs out, then the ups will cycle its outputs. Set this to zero to turns disable this feature.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsControl	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.4.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsControlTable	The actionable controls for each ups in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are upss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.4.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsControlEntry	An entry containing controls for a particular ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.4.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsControlSelfTest	Set to TRUE to initiate a self test on the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.4.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsControlRamp	Set to TRUE to initiate the pre-designated ramp sequence on the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.4.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsControlShed	Set to TRUE to initiate the pre-designated shed sequence on the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.4.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsControlUpsOn	Set to TRUE to turn the ups on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.4.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsControlUpsOff	Set to TRUE to turn the ups off.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.4.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsControlUpsReboot	Set to TRUE to reboot the ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.4.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsControlBypass	This switches the ups in and out of bypass mode. This value returns the current bypass mode: disable(0) if the ups is not in bypass mode, enable(1) if the ups is in bypass mode. Set to disable(0) to exit bypass mode, or enable(1) to enter bypass mode. If switching bypass mode is not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfig	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigTable	The configuration details of each ups in the device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of upss managed by the agent as reported by tlpUpsIdentNumUps.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigEntry	An entry containing information applicable to all input lines per each ups managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigInputVoltage	The nominal value of the input line voltage. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. This value may not be writable on all models. If not writable, the value will be rejected and an appropriate error message will be returned.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigBypassLowerLimitPercent	The lowest AC input voltage allowed to be output to the load while in bypass mode. This setting is expressed as a percentage from nominal voltage. If this value is not supported by the ups, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.11	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigBypassUpperLimitPercent	The highest AC input voltage allowed to be output to the load while in bypass mode. This setting is expressed as a percentage from nominal voltage. If this value is not supported by the ups, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.12	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigBypassLowerLimitVoltage	The lowest AC input voltage allowed to be output to the load while in bypass mode. If this value is not supported by the ups, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.13	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigBypassUpperLimitVoltage	The highest AC input voltage allowed to be output to the load while in bypass mode. If this value is not supported by the ups, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.14	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigColdStart	This option enables or disables the ability to turn the ups on without AC supplied. If this value is not supported by the ups, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.15	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigEconomicMode	The configurable economic mode options for the ups. The online(0) mode is the default configuration of most upss, which is synonymous as having the economic mode disabled. The economy(1) mode is the typical configuration to run in economy mode, which is synonymous as having the economic mode enabled. Constant50Hz(2) is a power strategy, which fixes the output frequency at 50Hz. Constant60Hz(3) is a power stragegy, which fixes the output frequency at 60Hz. ConstantAuto(4) regulates the output frequency at nominal input frequency. AutoAdaptive(5) mode will cause the ups to automatically switch between online(0), maximum quality, and economy(1), maximum efficiency, to improve efficiency during stable utility periods and improve output regulation during unstable utility periods. Not all values are supported by all upss. Most upss, if supportive of economic mode, only supports online(0) and economy(1). If the ups does not support economic mode, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.16	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigFaultAction	Determines the action to take if the output needs to be shut down due to a fault condition, limited by the type of fault incurred. When configured for bypass(0), the ups will go to bypass on a fault condition. When configured for standby(1), the ups will go to standby mode on a fault condition. Either configuration will be valid as long as AC input is within normal line voltage and frequency limits when the fault condition occurs. If the line is outside these limits, the ups will turn off. If this value is not supported by the ups, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.17	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigOffMode	This option governs what mode the ups should go into when AC input is available, but the load is either off or not battery backed up. If this setting is configured for bypass(1), the intention is that any time the ups would normally go into standby mode, it would instead go into bypass mode. Note that this setting does not dictate the mode for fault conditions, which is governed by tlpUpsConfigFaultAction. If this value is not supported by the ups, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.18	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigLineSensitivity	Adjusts the AC line voltage sensitivity setting. If this value is not supported by the ups, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigInputFrequency	The nominal input frequency. On those systems which support read-write access to this object, if there is an attempt to set this variable to a value that is not supported, the request must be rejected and the agent shall respond with an appropriate error message, i.e., badValue for SNMPv1, or inconsistentValue for SNMPv2.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigOutputVoltage	The nominal value of the output voltage. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, the agent reports ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. This value may not be writable on all models. If not writable, the value will be rejected and an appropriate error message will be returned.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigOutputFrequency	The nominal output frequency. On those systems which support read-write access to this object, if there is an attempt to set this variable to a value that is not supported, the request will be rejected and the agent will respond with an appropriate error message.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAudibleStatus	The requested state of the audible alarm. When in the disabled state, the audible alarm should never sound. The enabled state is self- describing. Setting this object to muted(3) when the audible alarm is sounding shall temporarily silence the alarm. It will remain muted until it would normally stop sounding and the value returned for read operations during this period shall equal muted(3). At the end of this period, the value shall revert to enabled(2). Writes of the value muted(3) when the audible alarm is not sounding shall be accepted but otherwise shall have no effect.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoBatteryTest	When disabled(0), the ups will not perform an automatic battery selftest. When set to another value, the ups will perform an automatic selftest in the approximate period defined by each respective enumerated value. This feature is generally not recommended.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoRestartAfterShutdown	When enabled(1), the ups should autorestart after a shutdown from battery mode if valid AC is applied. When disabled(0), the ups should not autorestart when AC is restored and instead power up into standby mode.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoRampOnTransition	When enabled(1), the ups should perform its preconfigured ramp sequence when valid AC is restored while in battery mode. If this value is not supported by the ups, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoShedOnTransition	When enabled(1), the ups should perform its preconfigured shed sequence when valid AC is lost causing the ups to enter battery mode. If this value is not supported by the ups, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoRestartTable	The configurable automatic restart options of each ups in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are upss. Not all options are available on all upss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoRestartEntry	An entry containing configurable automatic restart options for a particular ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoRestartInverterShutdown	If enabled(1) and the ups is turned off from invert mode (via user interaction), if line becomes valid, the ups will automatically go to line mode. If disabled(0), the ups will turn back on and go to standby mode instead.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoRestartDelayedWakeup	If enabled(1) and power fails during a DelayBeforeStartup and line remains invalid after the timeout expires, the ups will be set to turn back on automatically. If disabled(0), the ups will turn back on and go to standby mode instead.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoRestartLowVoltageCutoff	If enabled(1) and the ups is turned off from invert mode (via low voltage cutoff), if line becomes valid, the ups will automatically go to line mode. If disabled(0), the ups will turn back on and go to standby mode instead.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoRestartOverLoad	If enabled(1) and the ups is turned off from invert mode (via overload), if line becomes valid, the ups will automatically go to line mode. If disabled(0), the ups will turn back on and go to standby mode instead.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigAutoRestartOverTemperature	If enabled(1) and the ups is turned off from invert mode (via over temperature), if line becomes valid, the ups will automatically go to line mode. If disabled(0), the ups will turn back on and go to standby mode instead.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigThresholdTable	The configurable threshold options of each ups in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are upss. Not all options are available on all upss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigThresholdEntry	An entry containing configurable threshold options for a particular ups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigBatteryAgeThreshold	The number of months for a battery to be in service. The battery age alarm, tlpUpsAlarmBatteryAgeAboveThreshold, is triggered when the current date exceeds tlpUpsBatteryPackIdentInstallDate by tlpUpsConfigBatteryAgeThreshold months.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigLowBatteryThreshold	This value denotes the percentage of battery capacity remaining warning level. The low battery alarm, tlpUpsAlarmLowBattery, is triggered when tlpUpsEstimatedChargeRemaining drops below this value.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.3.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigLowBatteryTime	The value in seconds of tlpUpsEstimatedMinutesRemaining at which a lowBattery condition is declared. For agents which support only discrete (discontinuous) values, then the agent shall round up to the next supported value. If the requested value is larger than the largest supported value, then the largest supported value shall be selected.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.1.5.3.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpUpsConfigOverLoadThreshold	This value denotes the percentage of load at which the overload condition occurs. The overload alarm, tlpUpsAlarmOutputOverload, is triggered when the percentage of output load exceeds this value.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPdu	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdent	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentNumPdu	The number of pdu devices that this agent is currently managing.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentTable	The identity details of each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are pdus.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentEntry	An entry containing details for a particular pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentNumInputs	The number of input lines supported by the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentNumOutputs	The number of output lines supported by the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentNumPhases	The number of phases supported by the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentNumOutlets	The number of receptacles supported by the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentNumOutletGroups	The number of receptacle groups supported by the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentNumCircuits	The number of circuits supported by the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.2.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentNumBreakers	The number of bank breakers supported by the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.2.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduIdentNumHeatsinks	The number of heatsink thermistors supported by the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduSupportsTable	The supported details of each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are pdus.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduSupportsEntry	An entry containing supported details for a particular pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduSupportsEnergywise	Indicates whether the pdu supports Cisco EnergyWise.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduSupportsRampShed	Indicates whether the pdu supports ramping and shedding.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.3.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduSupportsOutletGroup	Indicates whether the pdu supports outlet groups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.3.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduSupportsOutletCurrentPower	Indicates whether the pdu reports individual receptacle current and power measurements. Devices that do not support individual receptacle measurements will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME for tlpPduOutletCurrent and tlpPduOutletPower.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.3.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduSupportsOutletVoltage	Indicates whether the pdu reports individual receptacle voltage measurements. Devices that do not support individual receptacle measurements will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME for tlpPduOutletVoltage.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDisplayTable	The display details of each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are pdus.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.4.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDisplayEntry	An entry containing display details for a particular pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.4.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDisplayScheme	Indicates the display scheme of the LED display. The value schemeReverse(0) indicates the tricolor LED indicator uses an alternate pattern. The value schemeNormal(1) indicates the LED indicator uses the standard pattern. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, the value will always return schemeNormal(1).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.4.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDisplayOrientation	Indicates the physical orientation of the LED display. The value displayNormal(0) indicates the display is right-side-up (normal). The value displayReverse(1) indicates the display is upside-down. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, the value will always return displayNormal(0).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.4.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDisplayAutoScroll	Indicates whether the LED display automatically scrolls through displaying status values.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.4.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDisplayIntensity	Indicates the intensity, as a percentage, of the LED display. The value intensity100(4) indicates the display is at 100% intensity. The other values indicate the display is at a lesser intensity based upon the respective percentage denoted.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.1.4.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDisplayUnits	Indicates the units of measurement displayed on the LED display. The value normal(0) indicates that a temperature value, for example, is displayed in degrees Farenheit. The value metric(1) indicates a temperature value is displayed in degrees Celsius.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDevice	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceTable	The device details of each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are pdus.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceEntry	An entry containing device details for a particular pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceMainLoadState	The current state of the main output of the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceAggregatePowerFactor	The aggregrate power factor of all phases.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.11	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceOutputCurrentPrecision	Output current is reported by tlpPduOutputCurrent, tlpPduOutputCurrentMin and tlpPduOutputCurrentMax. These values are all reported in hundredths (0.01A), which accommodates all models; however, on any given device the actual precision may vary. This value describes the actual precision, which can be used as a divisor against the output current values to obtain the true output current measurement. For example, if tlpPduOutputCurrent reports 530 and tlpPduDeviceOutputCurrentPrecision is tenths(1), then the actual output current is 5.3.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceMainLoadControllable	Indicates whether or not the main output is controllable, and whether the ups can be turned off and on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceMainLoadCommand	Reading this value will always return 0. Setting this value to turnOff(1) will turn off the main output of the ups. Setting this value to turnOn(2) will turn on the main output of the ups. Setting this value to cycle(3) will turn off the main output, then turn it back on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDevicePowerOnDelay	The configurable delay value, which sets the amount of additional time a given device will wait before it connects to a valid AC source. By default the delay value is set to 0. For devices with multiple AC input sources, this delay only applies to the primary input source.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceTotalInputPowerRating	The total input power rating of all phases on the device. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceTemperatureC	The ambient temperature at or near the PDU casing. Temperature measurements are not supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceTemperatureF	The ambient temperature at or near the PDU casing. Temperature measurements are not supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDevicePhaseImbalance	The percentage of imbalance of the three phases. This value is in the range from 0% imbalance to 100% imbalance. The lower the value, the better balanced the phases are. If all load is on a single phase, the imbalance is defined as 100%.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.2.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDeviceOutputPowerTotal	The AC output total power for all circuits.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduDetail	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInput	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputTable	The input details of each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the number of pdus managed by the agent as reported by tlpPduIdentNumPdus.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular pdu managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputNominalVoltage	The nominal value of the input line voltage. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputCurrentLimit	The capacity of each phase conductor in the pdu limited by the AC input cord or any other potential limiting factors unique to a given unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputNominalVoltagePhaseToPhase	The nominal value of the input line voltage as measured from phase to phase. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return zero.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputNominalVoltagePhaseToNeutral	The nominal value of the input line voltage as measured from phase to neutral. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return zero.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputLowTransferVoltage	The minimum line voltage allowed before the unit disconnects the AC input connection. This value may not be writable on all models. If not writable, the value will be rejected and an appropriate error message will be returned. When supported, the minimum and maximum values allowed are dictated by tlpPduInputLowTransferVoltageLowerBound and tlpPduInputLowTransferVoltageUpperBound respectively.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputLowTransferVoltageLowerBound	The lower boundary value of tlpPduInputLowTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputLowTransferVoltageUpperBound	The upper boundary value of tlpPduInputLowTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputHighTransferVoltage	The maximum line voltage allowed before the unit disconnects the AC input connection. This value may not be writable on all models. If not writable, the value will be rejected and an appropriate error message will be returned. When supported, the minimum and maximum values allowed are dictated by tlpPduInputHighTransferVoltageLowerBound and tlpPduInputHighTransferVoltageUpperBound respectively.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputHighTransferVoltageLowerBound	The lower boundary value of tlpPduInputHighTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputHighTransferVoltageUpperBound	The upper boundary value of tlpPduInputHighTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputPhaseTable	The input phase details of each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the value of tlpPduIdentNumInputs and tlpPduIdentNumPhases per each device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputPhaseEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular input phase managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputPhaseIndex	The table row index for the pdu phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputPhasePhaseType	Denotes whether measurements are phase to neutral(0) or phase to phase(1).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputPhaseFrequency	The present input frequency for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputPhaseVoltage	The magnitude of the present input voltage for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputPhaseVoltageMin	The minimum input voltage value since the last reset of this value for a given phase. If any value is written to either tlpPduInputVoltageMin or tlpPduInputVoltageMax, both will be reset to their appropriate minimum and maximum values.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputPhaseVoltageMax	The maximum input voltage value since the last reset of this value for a given phase. If any value is written to either tlpPduInputVoltageMin or tlpPduInputVoltageMax, both will be reset to their appropriate minimum and maximum values.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.1.2.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduInputPhaseCurrent	The magnitude of the present input current for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutput	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputTable	The output details of each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the value of tlpPduIdentNumOutputs per each device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputEntry	An entry containing output information applicable to a particular phase managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputIndex	The table row index for the pdu phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputSource	The present source of output power. The enumeration none(0) indicates that there is no source of output power (and therefore no output power), for example, the system has opened the output breaker.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputPhase	Indicates the phase associated with the output line.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputPhaseType	Denotes whether measurements are phase to neutral(0) or phase to phase(1).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputVoltage	The magnitude of the present output voltage for a given output line.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputCurrent	The output current, in hundreths of amps, for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputCurrentMin	The minimum current observed for a given phase since last reset.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputCurrentMax	The maximum current observed for a given phase since last reset.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputActivePower	The output power for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.2.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutputPowerFactor	The output power factor, in hundreths of a percent, for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutlet	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletTable	The receptacle status details of each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the value of tlpPduIdentNumOutlets per each device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular outlet managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletIndex	The table row index for the pdu outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletRampAction	The ramp action to take on a given outlet when powering on the device. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpPduOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.11	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletRampDelay	The number of seconds to delay before powering on the given outlet. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpPduOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.12	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletShedAction	The shed action to take on a given outlet when powering off the device. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpPduOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.13	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletShedDelay	The number of seconds to delay before powering off the given outlet. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpPduOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.14	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletGroup	The tlpPduOutletGroupIndex group index of the respective group to which the given outlet is assigned, or zero (0) if the given outlet is not grouped.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.15	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletBank	Indicates on which bank the given outlet is located.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.16	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletCircuit	Indicates on which circuit the given outlet is wired.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.17	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletPhase	Indicates on which phase or phases the given outlet is associated. For single phase devices, this object will always return phase1(1). For 3-phase devices with outlets wired to a single phase, this object will return phase1(1), phase2(2) or phase3(3). For 3-phase devices with outlets wired to two phases, this object will return phase1-2(4) for phases 1 and 2, phase2-3(5) for phases 2 and 3, and phase3-1(6) for phases 3 and 1. Devices that do not report phase connections will return unknown(0).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletName	A user-definable string identifying the name of the outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletDescription	A user-definable string identifying the device(s) connected to the given outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletState	The current state of the outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletControllable	Denotes whether this outlet is controllable.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletCommand	Reading this value will always return 0. Setting this value to turnOff(1) will turn off the outlet. Setting this value to turnOn(2) will turn on the outlet. Setting this value to cycle(3) will turn the outlet off, then turn it back on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletVoltage	The magnitude of the present output voltage for a given outlet. If the voltage measurement is not supported for an individual receptacle regardless whether device-wide or just for this receptacle, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. Device-wide support for receptacle voltage measurements is denoted by tlpPduSupportsOutletVoltage.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletCurrent	The present output current, in hundreths of amps, of a given outlet. If the current measurement is not supported for an individual receptacle regardless whether device-wide or just for this receptacle, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. Device-wide support for receptacle current measurements is denoted by tlpPduSupportsCurrentPower.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletPower	The output power of a given outlet. If the power measurement is not supported for an individual receptacle regardless whether device-wide or just for this receptacle, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. Device-wide support for receptacle power measurements is denoted by tlpPduSupportsCurrentPower.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletGroupTable	The receptacle grouping details of each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the value of tlpPduIdentNumOutletGroups per each device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletGroupEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular outlet group managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletGroupIndex	The table row index for the pdu outlet group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletGroupRowStatus	Row status for the tlpPduOutletGroupTable
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletGroupName	The name of this outlet group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletGroupDescription	A description for this outlet group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletGroupState	The current state of the outlet group. This value will report off(1) if all outlets in the group are off, on(2) if all outlets in the group are on, mixed(3) if some outlets in the group are off and others are on, or unknown(0) if the state of the outlets cannot be determined.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.3.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduOutletGroupCommand	Reading this value will always return 0. Setting this value to turnOff(1) will turn off every outlet associated with the group. Setting this value to turnOn(2) will turn on every outlet associated with the group. Setting this value to cycle(3) will turn off every outlet associated with the group, then turn each outlet back on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuit	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitTable	A list of pdu circuit table entries. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpPduIdentNumCircuits.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular circuit managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitIndex	The table row index for the pdu circuit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitUtilization	The percentage of utilization of a given circuit. This is typically a calculation of tlpPduCircuitTotalCurrent / tlpPduCircuitCurrentLimit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitPhase	Indicates on which phase or phases the given circuit is wired. For single phase devices, this object will always return phase1(1). For 3-phase devices with outlets wired to a single phase, this object will return phase1(1), phase2(2) or phase3(3). For 3-phase devices with outlets wired to two phases, this object will return phase1-2(4) for phases 1 and 2, phase2-3(5) for phases 2 and 3, and phase3-1(6) for phases 3 and 1. Devices that do not report phase connections will return unknown(0).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitInputVoltage	The input voltage for a circuit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitTotalCurrent	The total current for all receptacles in a given circuit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitCurrentLimit	The current capacity of a circuit in the system limited by the circuit breaker or wiring used in a given unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitCurrentMin	The minimum total current for all receptacles in a given circuit since last reset.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitCurrentMax	The maximum total current for all receptacles in a given circuit since last reset.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitTotalPower	The total power for all receptacles in a given circuit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.4.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduCircuitPowerFactor	The power factor for all receptacles in a given circuit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduBreaker	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.5.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduBreakerTable	A list of pdu bank breaker table entries. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpPduIdentNumBreakers.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.5.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduBreakerEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular bank breaker managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.5.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduBreakerIndex	The table row index for the pdu bank breaker.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.5.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduBreakerStatus	Indicates whether the bank breaker is open(0), closed(1) or not installed(2).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduHeatsink	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.6.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduHeatsinkTable	A list of pdu heatsink thermistor table entries. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpPduIdentNumHeatsinks.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.6.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduHeatsinkEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular heatsink thermistor managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.6.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduHeatsinkIndex	The table row index for the pdu heatsink thermistor.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.6.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduHeatsinkStatus	Indicates whether the heatsink thermistor is available. The entry will return notAvailable(0) if a thermistor is either non-existent or disconnected, or available(1) when connected.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.6.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduHeatsinkTemperatureC	The temperature at the heatsink termistor in tenths degrees Centigrade. Heatsink temperature measurements are not supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.3.6.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduHeatsinkTemperatureF	The temperature at the heatsink termistor in tenths degrees Farenheit. Heatsink temperature measurements are not supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduControl	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.4.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduControlTable	The actionable controls for each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are pdus.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.4.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduControlEntry	An entry containing controls for a particular pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.4.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduControlRamp	Set to TRUE to initiate the pre-designated ramp sequence on the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.4.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduControlShed	Set to TRUE to initiate the pre-designated shed sequence on the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.4.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduControlPduOn	Set to TRUE to turn the pdu on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.4.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduControlPduOff	Set to TRUE to turn the pdu off.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.4.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduControlPduReboot	Set to TRUE to reboot the pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduConfig	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.5.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduConfigTable	The configuration options of each pdu in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are pdus. Not all options are available on all pdus.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.5.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduConfigEntry	An entry containing configuration options for a particular pdu.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.2.5.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpPduConfigInputVoltage	The nominal value of the input line voltage. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. This value may not be writable on all models. If not writable, the value will be rejected and an appropriate error message will be returned.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvirosense	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvIdent	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvIdentNumEnvirosense	The number of envirosense devices that this agent is currently managing.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvIdentTable	The identity details of each envirosense in device table. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpDevicesNumDevices.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.1.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvIdentEntry	An entry containing details for a particular envirosense.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.1.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvIdentTempSupported	Indicates whether or not temperature is supported.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.1.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvIdentHumiditySupported	Indicates whether or not temperature is supported.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.1.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvNumInputContacts	The number of input contacts supported by the envirosense.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.1.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvNumOutputContacts	The number of output contacts supported by the envirosense.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvDetail	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvTemperatureTable	The temperature details of each envirosense in device table. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpDevicesNumDevices.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvTemperatureEntry	An entry containing temperature details for a particular envirosense.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvTemperatureC	The ambient temperature.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvTemperatureF	The ambient temperature.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvTemperatureInAlarm	Indicates whether or not temperature is in alarm.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvHumidityTable	The humidity details of each envirosense in device table. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpDevicesNumDevices.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvHumidityEntry	An entry containing humidity details for a particular envirosense.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvHumidityHumidity	The ambient humidity.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvHumidityInAlarm	Indicates whether or not humidity is in alarm.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvInputContactTable	The input contact details of each envirosense in device table. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpDevicesNumDevices.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvInputContactEntry	An entry containing input contact details for a particular envirosense.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvInputContactIndex	The table row index for the envirosense input contact details.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvInputContactName	The name or description of the contact.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.3.3.3.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpEnvInputContactNormalState	The normal operating position of the contact.
