.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsIdentTable	The identity details of each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are atss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsIdentEntry	An entry containing details for a particular ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsIdentNumInputs	The number of inputs supported by the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsIdentNumOutputs	The number of outputs supported by the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsIdentNumPhases	The number of phases per input supported by the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsIdentNumOutlets	The number of receptacles supported by the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsIdentNumOutletGroups	The number of receptacle groups supported by the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsIdentNumCircuits	The number of circuits supported by the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.2.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsIdentNumBreakers	The number of bank breakers supported by the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.2.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsIdentNumHeatsinks	The number of heatsink thermistors supported by the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsSupportsTable	The supported details of each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are atss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsSupportsEntry	An entry containing supported details for a particular ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsSupportsEnergywise	Indicates whether the ats supports Cisco EnergyWise.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsSupportsRampShed	Indicates whether the ats supports ramping and shedding.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.3.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsSupportsOutletGroup	Indicates whether the ats supports outlet groups.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.3.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsSupportsOutletCurrentPower	Indicates whether the ats reports individual receptacle current and power measurements. Devices that do not support individual receptacle measurements will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME for tlpAtsOutletCurrent and tlpAtsOutletPower.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.3.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsSupportsOutletVoltage	Indicates whether the ats reports individual receptacle voltage measurements. Devices that do not support individual receptacle measurements will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME for tlpAtsOutletVoltage.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDisplayTable	The display details of each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are atss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.4.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDisplayEntry	An entry containing display details for a particular ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.4.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDisplayScheme	Indicates the display scheme of the LED display. The value schemeReverse(0) indicates the tricolor LED indicator uses an alternate pattern. The value schemeNormal(1) indicates the LED indicator uses the standard pattern. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, the value will always return schemeNormal(1).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.4.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDisplayOrientation	Indicates the physical orientation of the LED display. The value displayNormal(0) indicates the display is right-side-up (normal). The value displayReverse(1) indicates the display is upside-down. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, the value will always return displayNormal(0).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.4.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDisplayAutoScroll	Indicates whether the LED display automatically scrolls through displaying status values.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.4.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDisplayIntensity	Indicates the intensity, as a percentage, of the LED display. The value intensity100(4) indicates the display is at 100% intensity. The other values indicate the display is at a lesser intensity based upon the respective percentage denoted.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.1.4.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDisplayUnits	Indicates the units of measurement displayed on the LED display. The value normal(0) indicates that a temperature value, for example, is displayed in degrees Farenheit. The value metric(1) indicates a temperature value is displayed in degrees Celsius.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDevice	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceTable	The device details of each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are atss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceEntry	An entry containing device details for a particular ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceMainLoadState	The current state of the main output of the device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceAggregatePowerFactor	The aggregrate power factor of all phases.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.11	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceOutputCurrentPrecision	Output current is reported by tlpAtsOutputCurrent, tlpAtsOutputCurrentMin and tlpAtsOutputCurrentMax. These values are all reported in hundredths (0.01A), which accommodates all models; however, on any given device the actual precision may vary. This value describes the actual precision, which can be used as a divisor against the output current values to obtain the true output current measurement. For example, if tlpAtsOutputCurrent reports 530 and tlpAtsDeviceOutputCurrentPrecision is tenths(1), then the actual output current is 5.3.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.12	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceGeneralFault	Indicates whether or not the ats is in a system fault condition. When the ats is in such a fault condition, the condition can be cleared with tlpAtsControlResetGeneralFault.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceMainLoadControllable	Indicates whether or not the main output is controllable, and whether the ups can be turned off and on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceMainLoadCommand	Reading this value will always return 0. Setting this value to turnOff(1) will turn off the main output of the ups. Setting this value to turnOn(2) will turn on the main output of the ups. Setting this value to cycle(3) will turn off the main output, then turn it back on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDevicePowerOnDelay	The configurable delay value, which sets the amount of additional time a given device will wait before it connects to a valid AC source. By default the delay value is set to 0. For devices with multiple AC input sources, this delay only applies to the primary input source.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceTotalInputPowerRating	The total input power rating of all phases on the device. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceTemperatureC	The ambient temperature at or near the ats casing. Temperature measurements are not supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceTemperatureF	The ambient temperature at or near the ats casing. Temperature measurements are not supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDevicePhaseImbalance	The percentage of imbalance of the three phases. This value is in the range from 0% imbalance to 100% imbalance. The lower the value, the better balanced the phases are. If all load is on a single phase, the imbalance is defined as 100%.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.2.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDeviceOutputPowerTotal	The AC output total power for all circuits.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsDetail	
