.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputFairVoltageThreshold	The voltage level at which the device will transition between sources.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.11	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputBadVoltageThreshold	The minimum line voltage allowed before the device disconnects the AC input connection.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.12	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputSourceAvailability	The determination as to which of two AC input lines are available. The agent will return either inputSourceA(1) or inputSourceB(2) if only one line is available, or inputSourceAB(3) if both lines are available. The agent will never return none(0) since the device will be powered off if neither line is available.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.13	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputSourceInUse	The determination as to which one of two AC input lines is in use. Not all devices support the reporting of which source is currently in use. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.14	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputSourceTransitionCount	The number of times the device transitions between primary and secondary sources. Most devices are limied to 65533 transitions, after which the value will not increment. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.15	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputCurrentLimit	The capacity of each phase conductor in the ats limited by the AC input cord or any other potential limiting factors unique to a given unit. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputNominalVoltagePhaseToPhase	The nominal value of the input line voltage as measured from phase to phase. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return zero.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputNominalVoltagePhaseToNeutral	The nominal value of the input line voltage as measured from phase to neutral. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return zero.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputBadTransferVoltage	The minimum line voltage allowed before the unit disconnects the AC input connection.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputBadTransferVoltageLowerBound	The lower boundary value of tlpAtsInputBadTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputBadTransferVoltageUpperBound	The upper boundary value of tlpAtsInputBadTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputHighTransferVoltage	The maximum line voltage allowed before the unit disconnects the AC input connection.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputHighTransferVoltageLowerBound	The lower boundary value of tlpAtsInputHighTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputHighTransferVoltageUpperBound	The upper boundary value of tlpAtsInputHighTransferVoltage as dictated by the hardware of the unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputPhaseTable	The input phase details of each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the value of tlpAtsIdentNumInputs and tlpAtsIdentNumPhases per each device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputPhaseEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular primary input phase managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputLineIndex	The table row index for the input line on the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputPhaseIndex	The table row index for the input phase for the input line.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputPhaseType	Denotes whether measurements are phase to neutral(0) or phase to phase(1).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputPhaseFrequency	The present input frequency for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputPhaseVoltage	The magnitude of the present input voltage for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputPhaseVoltageMin	The minimum input voltage value since the last reset of this value for a given phase. If any value is written to either tlpAtsInputVoltageMin or tlpAtsInputVoltageMax, both will be reset to their appropriate minimum and maximum values.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.2.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputPhaseVoltageMax	The maximum input voltage value since the last reset of this value for a given phase. If any value is written to either tlpAtsInputVoltageMin or tlpAtsInputVoltageMax, both will be reset to their appropriate minimum and maximum values.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.1.2.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsInputPhaseCurrent	The magnitude of the present input current for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutput	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputTable	The output details of each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the value of tlpAtsIdentNumOutputs per each device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputEntry	An entry containing output information applicable to a particular phase managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputIndex	The table row index for the ats phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputSource	The present source of output power. The enumeration none(0) indicates that there is no source of output power (and therefore no output power), for example, the system has opened the output breaker.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputPhase	Indicates the phase associated with the output line.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputPhaseType	Denotes whether measurements are phase to neutral(0) or phase to phase(1).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputVoltage	The magnitude of the present output voltage for a given output line.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputCurrent	The output current, in hundreths of amps, for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputCurrentMin	The minimum current observed for a given phase since last reset.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputCurrentMax	The maximum current observed for a given phase since last reset.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputActivePower	The output power for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.2.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutputPowerFactor	The output power factor, in hundreths of a percent, for a given phase.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutlet	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletTable	The receptacle status details of each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the value of tlpAtsIdentNumOutlets per each device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular outlet managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletIndex	The table row index for the ats outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletRampAction	The ramp action to take on a given outlet when powering on the device. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpAtsOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.11	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletRampDelay	The number of seconds to delay before powering on the given outlet. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpAtsOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.12	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletShedAction	The shed action to take on a given outlet when powering off the device. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpAtsOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.13	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletShedDelay	The number of seconds to delay before powering off the given outlet. If this receptacle is not controllable, as denoted by tlpAtsOutletControllable, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.14	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletGroup	The tlpAtsOutletGroupIndex group index of the respective group to which the given outlet is assigned, or zero (0) if the given outlet is not grouped.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.15	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletBank	Indicates on which bank the given outlet is located.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.16	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletCircuit	Indicates on which circuit the given outlet is wired.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.17	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletPhase	Indicates on which phase or phases the given outlet is associated. For single phase devices, this object will always return phase1(1). For 3-phase devices with outlets wired to a single phase, this object will return phase1(1), phase2(2) or phase3(3). For 3-phase devices with outlets wired to two phases, this object will return phase1-2(4) for phases 1 and 2, phase2-3(5) for phases 2 and 3, and phase3-1(6) for phases 3 and 1. Devices that do not report phase connections will return unknown(0).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletName	A user-definable string identifying the name of the outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletDescription	A user-definable string identifying the device(s) connected to the given outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletState	The current state of the outlet.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletControllable	Denotes whether this outlet is controllable.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletCommand	Reading this value will always return 0. Setting this value to turnOff(1) will turn off the outlet. Setting this value to turnOn(2) will turn on the outlet. Setting this value to cycle(3) will turn the outlet off, then turn it back on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletVoltage	The magnitude of the present output voltage for a given outlet. If the voltage measurement is not supported for an individual receptacle regardless whether device-wide or just for this receptacle, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. Device-wide support for receptacle voltage measurements is denoted by tlpAtsSupportsOutletVoltage.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletCurrent	The present output current, in hundreths of amps, of a given outlet. If the current measurement is not supported for an individual receptacle regardless whether device-wide or just for this receptacle, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. Device-wide support for receptacle current measurements is denoted by tlpAtsSupportsCurrentPower.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletPower	The output power of a given outlet. If the power measurement is not supported for an individual receptacle regardless whether device-wide or just for this receptacle, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. Device-wide support for receptacle power measurements is denoted by tlpAtsSupportsCurrentPower.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletGroupTable	The receptacle grouping details of each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain the number of entries based upon the value of tlpAtsIdentNumOutletGroups per each device.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletGroupEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular outlet group managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletGroupIndex	The table row index for the ats outlet group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletGroupRowStatus	Row status for the tlpAtsOutletGroupTable
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletGroupName	The name of this outlet group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletGroupDescription	A description for this outlet group.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletGroupState	The current state of the outlet group. This value will report off(1) if all outlets in the group are off, on(2) if all outlets in the group are on, mixed(3) if some outlets in the group are off and others are on, or unknown(0) if the state of the outlets cannot be determined.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.3.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsOutletGroupCommand	Reading this value will always return 0. Setting this value to turnOff(1) will turn off every outlet associated with the group. Setting this value to turnOn(2) will turn on every outlet associated with the group. Setting this value to cycle(3) will turn off every outlet associated with the group, then turn each outlet back on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuit	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitTable	A list of ats circuit table entries. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpAtsIdentNumCircuits.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular circuit managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitIndex	The table row index for the ats circuit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitUtilization	The percentage of utilization of a given circuit. This is typically a calculation of tlpAtsCircuitTotalCurrent / tlpAtsCircuitCurrentLimit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitPhase	Indicates on which phase or phases the given circuit is wired. For single phase devices, this object will always return phase1(1). For 3-phase devices with outlets wired to a single phase, this object will return phase1(1), phase2(2) or phase3(3). For 3-phase devices with outlets wired to two phases, this object will return phase1-2(4) for phases 1 and 2, phase2-3(5) for phases 2 and 3, and phase3-1(6) for phases 3 and 1. Devices that do not report phase connections will return unknown(0).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitInputVoltage	The input voltage for a circuit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitTotalCurrent	The total current for all receptacles in a given circuit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitCurrentLimit	The current capacity of a circuit in the system limited by the circuit breaker or wiring used in a given unit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitCurrentMin	The minimum total current for all receptacles in a given circuit since last reset.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitCurrentMax	The maximum total current for all receptacles in a given circuit since last reset.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitTotalPower	The total power for all receptacles in a given circuit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.4.1.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsCircuitPowerFactor	The power factor for all receptacles in a given circuit.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsBreaker	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.5.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsBreakerTable	A list of ats bank breaker table entries. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpAtsIdentNumBreakers.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.5.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsBreakerEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular bank breaker managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.5.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsBreakerIndex	The table row index for the ats bank breaker.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.5.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsBreakerStatus	Indicates whether the bank breaker is open(0), closed(1) or not installed(2).
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsHeatsink	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.6.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsHeatsinkTable	A list of ats heatsink thermistor table entries. The number of entries is given by the value of tlpAtsIdentNumHeatsinks.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.6.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsHeatsinkEntry	An entry containing information applicable to a particular heatsink thermistor managed by this agent.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.6.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsHeatsinkIndex	The table row index for the ats heatsink thermistor.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.6.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsHeatsinkStatus	Indicates whether the heatsink thermistor is available. The entry will return notAvailable(0) if a thermistor is either non-existent or disconnected, or available(1) when connected.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.6.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsHeatsinkTemperatureC	The temperature at the heatsink termistor in tenths degrees Centigrade. Heatsink temperature measurements are not supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.3.6.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsHeatsinkTemperatureF	The temperature at the heatsink termistor in tenths degrees Farenheit. Heatsink temperature measurements are not supported on all models. If not supported, this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsControl	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.4.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsControlTable	The actionable controls for each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are atss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.4.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsControlEntry	An entry containing controls for a particular ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.4.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsControlRamp	Set to TRUE to initiate the pre-designated ramp sequence on the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.4.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsControlShed	Set to TRUE to initiate the pre-designated shed sequence on the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.4.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsControlAtsOn	Set to TRUE to turn the ats on.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.4.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsControlAtsOff	Set to TRUE to turn the ats off.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.4.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsControlAtsReboot	Set to TRUE to reboot the ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.4.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsControlResetGeneralFault	Set to TRUE to reset the general fault alarm indicated by tlpAtsDeviceGeneralFault.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfig	
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigTable	The configuration options of each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are atss. Not all options are available on all atss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigEntry	An entry containing configuration options for a particular ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.1.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigInputVoltage	The nominal value of the input line voltage. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME. This value may not be writable on all models. If not writable, the value will be rejected and an appropriate error message will be returned.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.1.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSourceSelect	The determination as to which of two AC input lines is designated as the primary input source. The other is designated as the secondary input source. This value will always return inputSourceA(1) for devices with a single input source. Setting this value is supported only on selected models.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.1.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSource1ReturnTime	The nominal time to delay a transition to Source 1, if it is the preferred source.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.1.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSource2ReturnTime	The nominal time to delay a transition to Source 2, if it is the preferred source.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.1.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigAutoRampOnTransition	When enabled(1), the ats should perform its preconfigured ramp sequence when the input source transfers from its designated secondary source to its designated primary source. This value not supported on all ats devices. If not supported, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.1.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigAutoShedOnTransition	When enabled(1), the ats should perform its preconfigured shed sequence when the input source transfers from its designated primary source to its designated secondary source. This value not supported on all ats devices. If not supported, then this value will always return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigVoltageRangeTable	The voltage range options in this table is intended to configure the operating voltages of an ats. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are atss. All voltage points defined in this table are listed in a specific order from high to low. All voltage points must satsify the conditions and ranges defined for each point. Any point violating any of the relative limits will be rejected. For optimal operation, it is recommended that tlpAtsConfigHighVoltageReset be set lower than tlpAtsConfigHighVoltageTransfer by a margin no less than 1% of tlpAtsConfigHighVoltageTransfer; and that tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferReset (tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferReset) be set higher than tlpAtsConfigSource1BrownoutSet (tlpAtsConfigSource2BrownoutSet) by a margin no less than 1% of tlpAtsConfigSource1BrownoutSet (tlpAtsConfigSource2BrownoutSet). *The upper limit of line voltage is tlpAtsInputHighTransferVoltageUpperBound. The lower limit of line voltage is tlpAtsInputBadTransferVoltageLowerBound. All minimum and maximum limits for each voltage point are all exlusive unless indicated otherwise.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigVoltageRangeEntry	An entry containing voltage range configuration options for a particular ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigHighVoltageTransfer	The maximum line voltage allowed before the unit disconnects the AC input connection. The maximum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsInputHighTransferVoltageUpperBound (inclusively). The minimum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigHighVoltageReset. This value may not be configurable on all models. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1.10	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigLowVoltageTransfer	The minimum line voltage allowed before the unit disconnects the AC input connection. The maximum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigLowVoltageReset. The minimum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsInputBadTransferVoltageLowerBound (inclusively). If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigHighVoltageReset	If a unit is disconnected due to over-voltage, the line voltage has to fall below this value before the unit re-connects the AC input connection. The maximum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigHighVoltageTransfer. The minimum value allowed is dictated by the greater of tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferReset and tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferReset. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferReset	If input source 1 voltage level is above this value, a unit connected to source 2 will transition to source 1 (if it is the preferred source). The maximum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigHighVoltageReset. The minimum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigSource1BrownoutSet. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSource1BrownoutSet	This value dictates the voltage level below which source 1 goes into a brown out condition. The maximum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferReset. The minimum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferSet. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1.5	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferSet	If input source 1 voltage level falls below this value, a unit connected to source 1 will transition to source 2 (if it is in fair condition as denoted by tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferSet). The maximum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigSource1BrownoutSet. The minimum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigLowVoltageReset. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1.6	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferReset	If input source 2 voltage level is above this value, a unit connected to source 1 will transition to source 2 (if it is the preferred source). The maximum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigHighVoltageReset. The minimum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigSource2BrownoutSet. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1.7	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSource2BrownoutSet	This value dictates the voltage level below which source 2 goes into a brown out condition. The maximum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferReset. The minimum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferSet. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1.8	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferSet	If input source 2 voltage level falls below this value, a unit connected to source 2 will transition to source 1 (if it is in fair condition as denoted by tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferSet). The maximum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigSource2BrownoutSet. The minimum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigLowVoltageReset. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.2.1.9	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigLowVoltageReset	If a unit is disconnected due to under-voltage or is not powered up yet, the line voltage has to rise above this value before the unit gets connected to the AC input connection. The maximum value allowed is dictated by the lesser value of tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferSet and tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferSet. The minimum value allowed is dictated by tlpAtsConfigLowVoltageTransfer. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigVoltageRangeLimitsTable	The voltage range table, as documented by tlpAtsConfigVoltageRangeTable requires that all changes adhere with stack order, from high transfer voltage down to low transfer voltage. In addition to stack order, certain voltage range values have limits defining the absolute minimum and absolute maximum for such values. Any voltage value violating any respective limit defined herein will be rejected.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.3.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigVoltageRangeLimitsEntry	An entry containing voltage range limits configuration options for a particular ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.3.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSourceBrownoutSetMinimum	This value dictates the absolute lower limit by which tlpAtsConfigSource1BrownoutSet and tlpAtsConfigSource2BrownoutSet can be set. tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferSet and tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferSet, respectively, are also used when determining the lowest value a brownout value can be set at any given time. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.3.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSourceBrownoutSetMaximum	This value dictates the absolute upper limit by which tlpAtsConfigSource1BrownoutSet and tlpAtsConfigSource2BrownoutSet can be set. tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferReset and tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferReset, respectively, are also used when determining the greatest value a brownout value can be set at any given time. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.3.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSourceTransferSetMinimum	This value dictates the absolute lower limit by which tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferSet and tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferSet can be set. tlpAtsConfigLowVoltageReset is also used when determining the lowest value a transferset value can be set at any given time. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.3.1.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigSourceTransferSetMaximum	This value dictates the absolute upper limit by which tlpAtsConfigSource1TransferSet and tlpAtsConfigSource2TransferSet can be set. tlpAtsConfigSource1BrownoutSet and tlpAtsConfigSource2BrownoutSet, respectively, are also used when determining the greatest value a transferset value can be set at any given time. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.4	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigThresholdTable	The configurable threshold options of each ats in device table. This is a sparse dependent table, and will contain some subset of devices that are atss. Not all options are available on all atss.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.4.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigThresholdEntry	An entry containing configurable threshold options for a particular ats.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.4.1.1	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigOverCurrentThreshold	The output current measurement at which an over current condition is reported. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.4.1.2	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigOverTemperatureThreshold	The system temperature at which an over temperature condition is reported. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
.1.3.6.1.4.1.850.1.1.3.4.5.4.1.3	TRIPPLITE-PRODUCTS	tlpAtsConfigOverVoltageThreshold	The input voltage measurement at which an over voltage condition is reported. This value may not be supported on all models. If not supported, this value will return ERROR_NO_SUCH_NAME.
